  "result": "Perfect! All 327 tests pass. The refactoring is complete and successful.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Refactored src/invoices.js by moving totals-related functions to a new src/totals.js module:**\n\n**New src/totals.js contains:**\n- `lineTotal(line)` - calculates qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n- `lineDiscount(line)` - calculates discount amount with clamping\n- `lineVat(line)` - calculates VAT on discounted amount\n- `invoiceTotals(invoice)` - calculates all totals (subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total)\n\n**Maintained backward compatibility:**\n- src/invoices.js imports and re-exports all four functions\n- All existing code importing from src/invoices.js continues to work unchanged\n- No changes required to any other files\n\n**Added comprehensive test coverage:**\n- Created test/totals.test.js with 24 new tests\n- Tests cover:\n  - Basic calculations for qty, discount, VAT\n  - Edge cases (zero amounts, clamping, negative values)\n  - Multiple lines with different VAT rates\n  - Discount and voucher handling\n  - Banker's rounding precision\n  - Invoice totals with various line configurations\n\n**Benefits:**\n- src/invoices.js is now smaller and more focused\n- Totals logic is isolated in its own module\n- Easier to maintain and test specialized functionality\n- Clear separation of concerns",
